carol.png`, as the Carol identity reference.\n- Selected the candidate with exactly one Carol, a front door, an unfinished wall patch, a leaning ladder, an open paint can, and a brush.\n- Preserved the generated source under `$HOME/.codex/generated_images/019f3384-b1c4-7413-8049-bb6ee38a3a56/ig_07bf8f14ad802ac5016a4aa1fe4c4081969442b841e74bd58e.png`.\n- Resized the final workspace PNG to 1600 x 900.\n- Flattened the final workspace PNG to the established course palette: cornflower blue, black, white, cream, light gray, yellow, and orange.\n- `course-assets/` is ignored by git as regenerable course video output.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `file course-assets/scenes/module-02-lesson2B/m02_L2B_carol_scene.png` reports PNG image data at `1600 x 900`.\n- `sips -g pixelWidth -g pixelHeight course-assets/scenes/module-02-lesson2B/m02_L2B_carol_scene.png` reports `1600 x 900`.\n- Local Sharp color check reports 7 unique colors: `#040404`, `#61AEEB`, `#D9D9D9`, `#FF7A00`, `#FFD400`, `#FFF8CC`, and `#FFFFFF`.\n- Visual inspection confirms exactly one Carol with short curly light-gray hair, round glasses, a cream shirt, a frustrated fed-up expression, one sheet marked `LIEN`, a front door, unfinished wall patch, leaning ladder, open paint can, brush, no worker, no extra person, no clone, no ambient doodles, no other text, even blue margin, and nothing clipped at the edges.\n\n--- .planning/quick/260705-imz-generate-carol-lien-scene/PLAN.md ---\n---\nstatus: in-progress\ncreated: 2026-07-05\nbranch: claude/course-production\n---\n\n# Generate Carol lien scene asset\n\n## Goal\n\nGenerate the requested course scene PNG at `course-assets/scenes/module-02-lesson2B/m02_L2B_carol_scene.png`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Use `docs/design/style-ref-1.png` and `docs/design/style-ref-2.png` as exact flat sticker-sheet style references.\n- Use `docs/design/cast-board.png` and `course-assets/scenes/module-02-lesson2B/m02_L2B_carol.png` as Carol identity references.\n- Create one PNG at 1600 x 900.\n- Show exactly one full or half-length Carol: sixties, short curly light-gray hair, round glasses, cream shirt, pale near-white cream face, frustrated fed-up expression, pressed lips.\n- Place Carol just outside her own front door, holding one sheet of paper marked `LIEN`.\n- Include a half-finished abandoned repair beside her: leaning step ladder, open paint can with brush across it, and unfinished wall patch.\n- Keep a single flat cornflower-blue background and the established yellow, orange, cream, white, black, and light-gray palette.\n- Avoid any worker, second person, clone, reflection, extra text, ambient doodles, hearts, sparkles, music notes, speech bubbles, motion or emphasis marks, gradients, texture, shadows, lighting, and perspective grid.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Confirm the file exists at the requested path.\n- Confirm the file is a PNG and 1600 x 900.\n- Visually inspect for exactly one Carol, matching portrait identity and build.\n- Confirm `LIEN` is the only text.\n- Confirm the abandoned repair props are present and no worker or extra person appears.\n- Confirm the flat sticker-sheet style and even blue margin with nothing clipped.\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"019f388a-e537-7fa2-ab54-04463a0d997b"}}}
